      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65621,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lipoblastoma-like tumour of the vulva is most frequently a unilateral, grossly myxoid or gelatinous, well-defined, lobulated vulvar mass {25929353}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65622,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours characteristically show a lobulated growth delineated by variably sized septa and are composed of a mixture of mature adipocytes, univacuolated and bivacuolated lipoblasts, and cytologically bland spindle cells that have blunt-ended to tapered nuclei and ample fibrillary cytoplasm. There is a variably prominent myxoid matrix, and the vasculature is thin-walled and often branching, resembling vessels found in myxoid liposarcoma and lipoblastoma. Stromal collagen can be found as wispy fibres or robust plaques. Mitotic activity is infrequent and no necrosis is present {12047760; 25929353; 29976943}.</p>\r\n<p>The vast majority of tumours exhibit a lack of both PLAG1 and HMGA2, and either a complete loss or a mosaic pattern of weak and negative nuclear expression of RB1. They are negative for S100 and predominantly negative (or rarely focally positive) for MDM2 and CDK4 in the limited number of cases studied. Spindle cells may be positive for CD34.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65623,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65624,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The absence of <em>DDIT3</em> and <em>PLAG1</em> rearrangements (respectively) by FISH {25929353; 29976943} supports the distinction from myxoid liposarcoma and lipoblastoma. There is no evidence of <em>RB1</em> regional gain or loss by FISH, and there is a normal diploid profile in the majority of tumours by genomic copy-number analysis by chromosomal microarray {29976943}, suggesting the possibility that lipoblastoma-like tumour of the vulva may not be related to spindle cell lipoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65625,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> lobulated growth delineated by variably sized septa; admixture of mature adipocytes, univacuolated and bivacuolated lipoblasts, and bland spindle cells; variably myxoid matrix and thin-walled branching vasculature.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> no <em>DDIT3</em> or <em>PLAG1</em> rearrangements or <em>RB1</em> regional gain or loss by FISH; lack of PLAG1 and HMGA2 expression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65626,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65627,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 527,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours may infrequently recur, linked to resection margin involvement. Metastasis has not been reported {25929353}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:19:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
